    "faq_02": {
      "type": "section-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q_02_01": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "How do I measure my caravan mattress correctly?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Measure the <strong>width and length across the centre of your mattress in millimetres</strong>.</p><p>If your mattress has a head-end bolster, include the bolster in the <strong>total length measurement</strong>.</p><p>Also take note of the corner profile at the foot end of your mattress — <strong>rounded, square or cut corner</strong>.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_02": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Should I include the bolster when measuring my mattress?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Yes. If your mattress has a head-end bolster, include it in the total mattress length.</p><p>This allows us to recommend a topper that covers both the main mattress and bolster where appropriate.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_03": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "What is a mattress bolster?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>A bolster is an additional section of mattress, usually positioned at the head end, that allows the bed to extend when in use and retract when more space is needed inside the caravan.</p><p>When measuring for a topper, include the bolster in your total mattress length.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_04": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "How should I position my mattress topper on a bed with a bolster?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>For mattresses with a bolster, we generally recommend covering both the main mattress and the bolster where possible.</p><p>Position the topper flush with the bolster at the head of the bed and secure the corner straps at that end. When the bed base is retracted and the bolster lifts during the day, the topper will flex and curve upwards with your bedding.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_05": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "My mattress is called a Queen, Double or Single. Is that enough to choose a topper?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>No. Caravan mattress dimensions can vary considerably between manufacturers, models and year ranges.</p><p>Always measure your mattress before ordering rather than relying on the mattress name alone.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_06": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "What if my mattress doesn’t exactly match one of your topper sizes?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>That’s very common.</p><p>A topper does not need to match your mattress millimetre for millimetre. We generally look for the closest fit while avoiding excessive overhang.</p><p>In many cases, a topper that is slightly smaller than the mattress is preferable to one that hangs over the edges.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_07": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Will a topper fit my mattress shape?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Most likely! Our Wanderluxe™ range includes a variety of sizes and corner profiles designed to suit many of the different caravan bed shapes found across Australia.</p><p>Rounded-corner toppers can work well on rounded, square and many cut-corner mattresses, while a slightly smaller topper is generally preferable to one that overhangs your mattress or interferes with surrounding cabinetry.</p><p>If your mattress is angled, varies in width or has an unusual shape, enter your measurements into our <a href=\"/pages/find-your-fit\">Sizing Calculator</a> or send them through to our Customer Care team and we’ll help you find the best fit.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_08": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Is it better for a topper to be slightly smaller or slightly larger than my mattress?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Slightly smaller is generally preferable.</p><p>A small shortfall around the edges is unlikely to affect comfort, whereas excessive overhang can allow the foam to move, compress or interfere with surrounding cabinetry.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_09": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Will a small gap at the foot end affect comfort?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Usually not.</p><p>A small length shortfall at the foot end is generally less important than getting the width right and avoiding overhang.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_10": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Why is mattress width so important?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>We recommend matching the <strong>width</strong> of your mattress before the length, as any shortfall across the width is more likely to be noticed — especially when two people are sharing the bed.</p><p>A small difference in length is usually easier to accommodate, as any shortfall at the foot end is less likely to affect comfort.</p><p>Once you’ve matched the width as closely as possible, check the overall fit and avoid excessive overhang in either direction. A small amount of overhang may be acceptable, but less is generally better.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_11": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Can I use a rounded-corner topper on a square mattress?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Yes. It’s very common to use a rounded-corner topper on a square-corner mattress.</p><p>There may be a small gap at the square corners, but this is typically unnoticeable once your bedding is fitted.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_12": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Can I use a square-corner topper on a rounded mattress?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>We generally don’t recommend it, as the square corners may extend beyond the rounded mattress underneath.</p><p>A rounded topper is usually the better option for a rounded mattress.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_13": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "What if my mattress has cut or angled corners?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Many cut-corner mattresses can be matched with one of our rounded-corner toppers.</p><p>Enter your dimensions and corner profile into our <a href=\"/pages/find-your-fit\">Sizing Calculator</a>, or contact our Customer Care team if you’re unsure.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_14": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "What if my mattress is wider at one end than the other?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Measure the mattress across the centre and provide any additional dimensions that may affect the fit.</p><p>If the shape is unusual, contact our <a href=\"/pages/contact\">Customer Care team</a> with your measurements and, if helpful, photos of the mattress so we can assist.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_15": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "My mattress sits tightly between walls or cabinetry. Does this affect sizing?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Yes. If your mattress sits within a tight bed frame or between cabinetry, it is particularly important to avoid choosing a topper that is too wide.</p><p>A slightly smaller topper is generally preferable to one that needs to be compressed into the available space.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_16": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "My measurements are in between two topper sizes. Which should I choose?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>The best option depends on the width, length and corner profile of your mattress.</p><p>As a general rule, we prefer to avoid overhang and will often recommend the slightly smaller option where two sizes are close.</p><p>Our <a href=\"/pages/find-your-fit\">Sizing Calculator</a> can help narrow this down, or our Customer Care team can assist.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_17": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Should I wait until I have access to my caravan before ordering?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p><strong>Yes, we recommend waiting until you can physically measure your mattress!</strong></p><p>Mattress dimensions and corner profiles can vary even between caravans of the same make or model. Waiting until you have access to your caravan means you can take accurate measurements with a measuring tape and check the corner profile at the foot end before placing your order.</p><p>This gives you the best chance of finding the right fit and avoiding unnecessary returns.</p><p>For full details on returns, head on over to our <a href=\"/policies/refund-policy\">Returns Policy</a> page.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_02_18": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Can you recommend a topper based on my caravan make and model?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p><strong>No</strong>. Caravan mattress sizes, shapes and profiles can vary between models and years, and manufacturers may also change their specifications over time. With so many different configurations available, we’re unable to maintain a complete and reliable list based on caravan make and model alone.</p><p>For the most accurate recommendation, we always recommend measuring your actual mattress and choosing your topper based on its <strong>width, length and corner profile</strong>.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        }
      },
