    "faq_03": {
      "type": "section-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q_03_01": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Will the topper work with a bolster-style mattress?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Yes. Our range includes longer topper sizes that can suit mattresses with bolsters.</p><p>If your bed retracts and the bolster lifts during the day, the memory foam can flex and lift with the mattress, similar to your bedding.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_03_02": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Should the topper cover the bolster?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Where possible, yes. We recommend including the bolster in your total mattress length so the topper can cover the complete sleep surface.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_03_03": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Can I use a Wanderluxe™ Mattress Topper on a folding or hybrid bed?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Yes. Many customers use Wanderluxe™ Toppers with folding beds, hybrid beds and camper trailers.</p><p>The memory foam is soft and flexible, provided there is enough room for the topper to fold comfortably within the bed cavity. For long periods of non-use, we recommend removing the topper and storing it flat or gently rolled rather than leaving it folded or compressed.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_03_04": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Can I leave the topper folded when the caravan isn’t being used?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>Short-term folding while travelling is generally fine.</p><p>For extended storage periods of around a month or more, we recommend removing the topper and storing it flat or gently rolled rather than leaving it folded or compressed.</p><p>If it has been folded or compressed for more than a day or two, allow up to <strong>12 hours</strong> for the memory foam to fully regain its shape before use.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_03_05": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Will a topper hide a join or fold in a split mattress?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>A topper can help create a more continuous sleep surface over a split or folding mattress, but the result will depend on the condition and structure of the mattress underneath.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        },
        "q_03_06": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "faq_question": "Will a topper fix a dip, ridge or sag in my mattress?",
            "icon": "none",
            "header_image_width": 25,
            "faq_answer": "<p>A Wanderluxe™ Topper can add cushioning and comfort to a firm, flat mattress, but it cannot correct structural issues such as significant sagging, deep dips or an uneven mattress base.</p>",
            "page": "",
            "image_width": 465,
            "liquid": "",
            "html": "",
            "show_contact_form": false
          }
        }
      },
